+// WHAT A SHOPPER SEES WHEN A PAYMENT CANNOT START. The storefront sends the browser here by a top-level
+// navigation, so every refusal below is a page, not an API answer; it used to be one bare ENGLISH line with
+// no way back, on an Arabic-first shop (?lang=ar made no difference). Arabic unless ?lang=en, the project's
+// language rule; same status codes, same Retry-After, no script.
+function cbk_fail_page(int $status, string $en, string $ar): never
+{
+    $isEn = strtolower(trim((string) (($_POST + $_GET)['lang'] ?? ''))) === 'en';
+    http_response_code($status);
