+// Give back the attempt that cbk_attempt_ref() just took, because the bank was
+// never reached (Authenticate failed). Measured: ten failed starts during a CBK
+// outage left pay_attempt = 10 on an order that had never touched the bank, and
+// the eleventh start, with CBK healthy again, was refused "Too many payment
+// attempts. Start a new checkout." The ceiling exists to stop a loop hammering
+// the bank, and a start that never reached the bank has not hammered it.
+// Guarded so it never goes below zero and only touches a still-pending order.
+function cbk_attempt_refund(array $cfg, string $trackid): void
+{
+    try {
+        cbk_pdo($cfg)->prepare(
+            "update orders set pay_attempt = greatest(pay_attempt - 1, 0)
+              where track_id = ? and payment_status = 'pending' and pay_attempt > 0"
